    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Situated in a quiet cul de Sac in Portobello this double fronted two bedroom red brick house presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a period property where architectural excellence and contemporary living combine to provide a home that delivers every comfort. This house was meticulously renovated and extended to an excellent standard with RMA Architects in 2023 and is filled with natural light throughout. The layout of the house flows well and no expense was spared in creating a space that combines design, functionality and comfort. Viewing is recommended!\r\n\r\nThe flooring, which features underfloor heating, throughout the house is polished concrete which contributes to the flow and harmony within the property.  An entrance hallway leads to the living room with a vaulted ceiling with two Velux windows and a large window overlooking the garden.  A Crittall door leads to the kitchen.  This room’s main feature is the rear wall which is fitted with a solid oak slatted wall panel cleverly concealing a fridge freezer, walk-in larder and a utility room.  The larder has custom built shelving.  The utility room has custom built storage and plumbing for a washing machine and tumble dryer.  The kitchen is by Colin Maher and is fitted with a range of wall and floor units with quartz worktops, Quooker tap and integrated appliances including a Bora downdraft hob, Bosch oven and Bosch dishwasher.  The room is lit by a pendant roof light, recessed under cabinet lighting, spot lights and a roof light and sliding door.  Off the living room is a cloakroom lit with a  pendant light in a vaulted ceiling and fitted with custom built storage for coats and shoes.  The cloakroom has a pocket door leading to the bathroom which has a vaulted ceiling and electric Velux window.  The bathroom is finished in a bold contemporary colour scheme of orange, black and white and features a heated towel rail and Hansgrohe bathroom accessories.  The master bedroom is to the front of the house on one side of the hallway and on the other side is the second bedroom with built-in floor to ceiling storage. Both bedrooms and electric blackout blinds and hardwood shutters.  Outside is a rear garden paved with Italian porcelain tiles.  The garden is plumbed and has outdoor electric sockets, lighting, shed and a timber storage unit.\r\n\r\nPortobello is a quiet residential area situated close to the Royal Canal.  It is host to a choice of eateries including Lennox Street Grocer, Brindle and Alma café.  It is a short walk to bustling Camden Street, a thoroughfare where you will find a range of cafés, grocery shops, restaurants and pubs.  Grafton Street and St Stephen’s Green are approximately 10 minutes away on foot.  The area is served by the Luas green line and Dublin Bus.  A dublinbikes station is located on Portobello Road."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hall     3.55m x 0.87m\r\nPolished concrete floor.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1     3.50m x 2.87m\r\nPolished concrete floor. Blackout electric blind and shutters.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2     3.46m x 2.98m\r\nPolished concrete floor. Blackout electric blind and shutters. Built-in floor to ceiling wardrobes.\r\n\r\nLiving room     4.87m x 3.04m\r\nPolished concrete floor. Vaulted ceiling. 2 Velux windows. Crittall door leading to kitchen.\r\n\r\nKitchen     3.52m x 3.27m\r\nPolished concrete floor. Solid oak slatted wall panel. Range of wall and floor units. Quartz worktops. Integrated fridge freezer, Bora downdraft hob, Bosch oven and Bosch dishwasher. Sliding door to rear garden. \r\n\r\nLarder     1.37m x 1.22m\r\nPolished concrete floor. Built-in shelving.\r\n\r\nUtility room     2.08m x 1.27m\r\nPolished concrete floor. Plumbing for washing machine and tumble dryer. Built-in storage.\r\n\r\nCloakroom     2.04m x 0.79m\r\nPolished concrete floor. Vaulted ceiling. Built-in cupboards.\r\n\r\nBathroom     2.03m x 1.79m\r\nPolished concrete floor. Vaulted ceiling. Recessed lighting. Electric Velux window. WC. Bath with shower overhead with Monsoon shower head. Wash hand basin. Heated towel rail. Hansgrohe bathroom accessories.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nRear garden     4.74m x 3.17m\r\nItalian porcelain tile paving, garden shed, plumbing, electric sockets, lighting, shed and timber storage unit.\r\n\r\nOn street permit parking to front."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "BER B3\r\nFully refurbished and extended in 2023\r\nFloor area approximately 63sqm/678sqft with a 15sqm/161sqft courtyard \r\nEV charging point \r\nHardwood sash windows and doors by Greenwood Joinery \r\nVindr Window and sliding door to in the kitchen \r\nGoogle Smart home technology throughout (Google Nest doorbell, fire/monoxide alarms, thermostats, speakers in living room, bathroom and kitchen).\r\nPolished concrete floor throughout \r\nZoned underfloor heating throughout\r\nBuster & Punch switches, door hinges and handles\r\nUSB A & C compatible sockets throughout \r\nHans Grohe bathroom accessories \r\nColin Maher custom kitchen \r\nRear garden with Italian porcelain tiles, plumbing & electricity points\r\n30sqm floored attic storage space \r\nBlackout electric blinds and hardwood shutters in each bedroom"
      },
      {
